// A new rule: a cell is born only next to exactly one neighbour, and nothing survives.
name Spark
rule B1/S
steps 3
hint A different law now. Each cell lives for one generation and only lonely neighbours light up. Explore: the rings are out there.
tip The four rings sit two cells diagonally from where the spark was. The spark cell itself is empty now.
intro The law changes underfoot. Here nothing lived past its first breath, and only the lonely were born.
outro A spark leaves rings. The spark itself is gone.
